@api = http://localhost:5093/api

### 1. Listar clientes (200)
GET {{api}}/customers?page=1&pageSize=20
Accept: application/json

### 2. Crear cliente (201)
POST {{api}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "María López",
  "phone": "9999-0000",
  "email": "maria@correo.com"
}

### 3. Crear cliente sin nombre (400)
POST {{api}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "",
  "phone": "9999-0000"
}

### 4. Buscar por nombre o teléfono (200)
GET {{api}}/customers?search=María
Accept: application/json

### 5. Crear otro cliente y guardar su id (201)
# @name crear
POST {{api}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Carlos Mejía",
  "phone": "8888-1111",
  "email": "carlos@correo.com"
}

### 6. Consultar por Id (200)
GET {{api}}/customers/{{crear.response.body.id}}

### 7. Consultar un Id que no existe (404)
GET {{api}}/customers/0192f000-0000-7000-8000-000000000999

### 8. Editar el cliente (204)
PUT {{api}}/customers/{{crear.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Carlos Mejía Rodríguez",
  "phone": "8888-2222",
  "email": "carlos@correo.com"
}

### 9. Editar con correo inválido (400)
PUT {{api}}/customers/{{crear.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Carlos",
  "phone": "8888-2222",
  "email": "esto-no-es-correo"
}